00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:58.420
<b>Hope</b>

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:01.570
Captain, we can now switch to aerodynamic control.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.770
Deploy the main wings! Be extra careful!

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:07.700
Deploying main wings. Switching to atmospheric flight.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:11.960
How are communications and sensors?

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:15.880
Offline. Radio waves are unreliable due to the falling fragments.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.880
Well, use lasers or thermal sensors or something!

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:20.430
We need to find the Impulse and ZAKU!

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:24.100
Are you suggesting that they've descended safely?

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:30.230
You may find this strange after I fired the Tannhauser without hesitation,

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:32.060
but I want to believe they're all right.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:44.890
Without a booster, I guess there's just no way to enter the atmosphere!

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:46.830
<i>Athrun! Athrun!</i>

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:48.710
Is that you, Shinn?!

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:49.750
<i>Stay where you are! I'll be right there!</i>

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:52.860
Stop it! Even the Impulse doesn't have enough thrust

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:54.920
to withstand the fall of two machines!

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.380
<i>Why must you always insist on telling us what can't be done?</i>

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:04.250
Then what would you rather I tell you?

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:06.480
<i>Something like, "Help me, you bastard!"</i>

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:09.430
Would you prefer that?

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:12.240
<i>No. That's just an example</i>.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:16.480
Sensors have picked up something! Seven o'clock, distance 400!

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:17.840
It's...

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:20.570
The Impulse? No.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:22.670
Can you bring up a visual?

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:24.340
Yes! In a moment!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.410
The ZAKU is okay too.

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:30.580
Athrun...

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:33.810
Arthur. Give them a sign using the signal flares.

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:34.570
Yes, ma'am!

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:36.000
Malik, take us to them.

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:41.000
We'd better catch them quickly, or they'll both hit the ocean's surface.

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:52.770
The Impulse and ZAKU have landed.

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:01.780
Athrun!

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:09.520
Wh-What? What is it now?

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:13.410
That's the impact of the first fragments after traveling full circle around the world.

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:14.860
Most likely.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:33.420
Rome. Shanghai. The Gobi Desert. Quebec.

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:36.200
Philadelphia and the North Atlantic.

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:39.620
There's no way of telling how high the number of casualties could climb.

00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:41.920
A tragedy beyond words.

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:46.030
But the real problems begin now.

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:56.830
Approach angle, satisfactory. Flaps down.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.780
Calculating estimated ocean surface wind velocity.

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:05.880
Water landing checklist one through twenty-four, all clear.

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:12.680
The ground effect is higher than in the simulations!

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:13.970
Adjust for it!

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:18.640
Attention! All units, brace for water-landing!

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:42.630
<i>We have landed safely</i>. <i>Reverting to normal status</i>.

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:46.770
<i>All sections checked and no leaks currently detected,</i>

00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:48.470
<i>but we will continue to watch for them</i>.

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:51.620
Damage control staff, make your way to the lower sections.

00:11:58.420 --> 00:12:00.230
So we're on Earth.

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:05.150
I think we've landed in what they call the Pacific Ocean. It's enormous!

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:08.150
We're not here on vacation, you know.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:11.030
Why are you always like that?

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:13.540
Are you all right, Athrun?

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:15.860
Yeah. I'm fine.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:21.150
But what a surprise. I was so worried.

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:24.120
You never said anything about going out in a mobile suit.

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:26.880
Sorry about that, acting on my own.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:31.300
It's okay. I have no problem with that. I know your abilities.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:35.760
In fact I'm kinda glad you did go out.

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:41.950
Although what's happened is extremely unfortunate,

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:46.200
if it wasn't for the Minerva and Yzak's team, it would've been a lot worse to say the least.

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:49.610
I'm sure the people of Earth understand that.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:51.030
Enough of your blabbering!

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:54.870
Oh, no. Not again.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:59.540
You were on the bridge! So I'm sure you know what really took place here!

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:01.890
Shinn!

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:05.540
The fall of Junius Seven wasn't an accident!

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:08.840
There were people behind this! The ones who did it were Coordinators!

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:12.430
Men whose families were killed there

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:14.430
and who still hold a grudge about the incident!

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:16.850
They dropped that thing, saying "Naturals should perish!"

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:46.280
I-I know that! I know about that... but still...

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:47.130
But what?!

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:51.210
You guys did everything you could to try to stop it!

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:52.470
Of course we did!

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:59.390
And yet its fragments are still wreaking devastation upon Earth.

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:10.780
We couldn't stop it completely!

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:12.440
Athrun...

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:32.320
Even though it was done by only a handful of people,

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:36.930
the fact remains that we Coordinators were responsible for this.

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:43.270
Do you think the people will forgive us with that in mind?

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.780
The last thing said by the leader of the men who self detonated was:

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:03.540
"For us Coordinators, the path of Patrick Zala was the one and only correct path!"

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:22.160
Athrun...

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:24.770
You really have no idea about anything, do you?!

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:34.940
I feel sorry for him!

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:45.060
<i>We at the PLANTs cannot express the great sorrow we feel concerning this calamity of unprecedented proportions</i>.

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:51.500
<i>I personally have no words to express how shocked I am to see the scenes of devastation from around the world</i>.

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:57.240
<i>Oh boy. A lot of damage has been done after all</i>.

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:01.820
<i>Even the Parthenon has been blown away</i>.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:08.030
The world won't change just because some old ruin disappeared.

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:10.850
<i>So, what happens now, Djibril?</i>

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:16.310
<i>I'm sure that the resulting scars are deep and there is no end in sight to your sorrow,</i>

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:19.200
<i>but please, my friends on Earth</i>...

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:22.480
<i>Please rise from the despair of this day</i>.

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:29.120
<i>We are committed to doing everything we can to help you through this unimaginable hardship</i>.

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:32.080
<i>Durandal certainly takes action quickly</i>.

00:16:32.690 --> 00:16:38.590
<i>He's already taking steps to help while giving us a bunch of sweet talk</i>.

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:42.890
I believe you should all be receiving a copy of something right about now.

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:47.560
Phantom Pain has sent us something very interesting.

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:50.940
<i>Why, this is</i>...

00:16:51.640 --> 00:16:52.980
<i>Hey! What in the world?!</i>

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:55.210
<i>Flare motors?!</i>

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:58.610
<i>Well, well. So that's what happened</i>.

00:16:58.610 --> 00:17:00.780
This unexpected trump card is perfect.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:05.620
Not one human being in the world will forgive them for what is shown here.

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:10.580
And it will allow us to form strong ties with the people like nothing else could.

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:15.630
This time for sure, we'll send all of those bastards to their deaths!

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:19.510
For the preservation of our blue and pure world.

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:28.180
<i>Why can't you realize</i>...

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:37.150
...<i>that for us Coordinators, the path of Patrick Zala was the one and only correct path!</i>

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:47.160
As expected, nothing.

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:50.950
The particle density is too great. Not even laser communication is possible right now.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:53.680
I see. Thanks.

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:54.440
No problem.

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:08.690
We are planning to proceed to Orb as soon as we're done checking the ship and have cleared emergency matters.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.500
Yeah, I know.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:15.980
I understand that there's no point in talking to them from where we are.

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:17.980
I do understand that, but...

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:23.650
Orb is an island nation after all. It's only natural you'd be worried.

00:18:27.140 --> 00:18:33.840
As a token of my appreciation for your distinguished service, let me know if there's anything I can do for the Minerva.

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:36.830
But at this point, I can't make any promises.

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:38.880
Please forgive me, Captain.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:41.440
No. There's no need to apologize.

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:03.150
Oh, it's you.

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:04.320
Mandatory training?

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:08.300
Yes. If we're going to anyway, they said it would probably be more refreshing outside.

00:19:08.800 --> 00:19:10.240
But I'm not doing too well.

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:21.460
Won't you join us?

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:23.380
No, I'll pass.

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:30.430
The truth is, we all know quite a bit about you.

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:34.100
Formerly a ZAFT Red, with the Le Creuset Team.

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:38.140
In the middle stages of the war, you defeated the Strike, said to be the strongest.

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:39.480
After that,

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:42.820
you were assigned to the FAITH special forces team which reported directly to the National Defense Committee.

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:48.580
Then you became the pilot of the ZGMF X09A Justice.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:49.990
You're Athrun Zala.

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:57.700
I don't know too much about your father, but you're quite a hero among us.

00:19:58.200 --> 00:20:00.710
Especially what you did at the battle of Jachin Due.

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:03.130
Ah, well...

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:07.320
And I hear you're quite skilled with a gun as well.

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:19.600
Can you show us a bit? The truth is, I'm not too good at this.

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:46.240
Wow! You're using the same gun, but what a difference!

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:53.140
It's not the gun. You have a habit of twisting your wrist as you pull the trigger.

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:55.840
That's why your spacing is inconsistent.

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:57.060
Athrun?

00:20:59.840 --> 00:21:03.320
Although, it's pretty useless to be good at things like this.

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:05.940
I disagree.

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:09.860
It's necessary to protect yourself and your friends from the enemy.

00:21:12.220 --> 00:21:14.320
And who's that enemy?

00:21:16.680 --> 00:21:19.410
I hear the Minerva's heading to Orb.

00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:29.840
Will you also be returning to Orb?

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:31.780
Yeah.

00:21:32.460 --> 00:21:33.300
Why is that?

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:38.390
What do you do there?

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:48.640
A storm is on its way.{a shitstorm's a brewin}

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:51.380
Yeah. I know.

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:59.540
<b>tooku hanareteru hodo ni chikaku ni kanjiteru</b>

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:59.540
<b>The further we are apart, the nearer I feel you are</b>

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:10.210
<b>samishisa mo tsuyosa eto kawatteku... kimi wo omottanara</b>

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:10.210
<b>Even my loneliness turns into strength... when I think of you</b>

00:22:18.050 --> 00:22:25.480
<b>kotoba wo kasanete mo wakari aenai koto</b>

00:22:18.050 --> 00:22:25.480
I still did not realize

00:22:24.770 --> 00:22:32.280
<b>
mada shiranakatta ne</b>

00:22:24.770 --> 00:22:32.280
That there are things that can't be conveyed even with words

00:22:31.570 --> 00:22:39.910
<b>kimi dake wo dakishimetakute nakushita yume kimi wa</b>

00:22:31.570 --> 00:22:39.910
My lost dreams of wanting to hold you by my side,

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:46.870
<b>
"akiramenaide" to itta</b>

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:46.870
For them, you said, "Don't give up!"

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:53.710
<b>tooku hanareteru hodo ni chikaku ni kanjiteru</b>

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:53.710
The further we are apart, the nearer I feel you are

00:22:53.010 --> 00:23:01.850
<b>
samishisa mo tsuyosa eto kawatteku... kimi wo omottanara</b>

00:22:53.010 --> 00:23:01.850
Even my loneliness turns into strength... when I think of you

00:23:01.180 --> 00:23:08.560
<b>setsunaku mune wo sasu sore wa yume no kakera</b>

